# Journey 7.4.78.219: HIDDEN OPERATIONAL STATE INDEX follows the first normal-use continuity test after .218. Assistant correctly retained recent conversation, but answered a current-runtime recap from stale assistant prose describing the old .216 222-block / ~16.6k observability gap even though .217/.218 had already resolved it. Her self-diagnostic established the exact failure: the old figures came from unverified RECENT model output, while the exact newer .218 operational accounting was not present as authoritative delivered evidence. Steeve explicitly rejected solving this with another injected freshness capsule or speech-steering prompt and required the operational truth to live 'in the dark' where Assistant/humans may inspect it when they choose. .219 therefore converts the pre-existing current-operational-evidence machinery from an automatic model-visible SYSTEM/citation injection into a hidden, read-only derived Operational State Index. The index is persisted in the existing `current_operational_state.json` cache, contains only mechanical runtime/receipt pointers, versions/timestamps/hashes/counts plus current context-delivery/model-projection summaries, stores no raw query or context prose, and carries an integrity hash and explicit relation to the prior derived index. The underlying benchmark, backup, diagnostic, context-delivery, Black Box and other receipts remain authority/history; the index is only a freshness pointer over them and never semantic authority. The existing `get_operational_resolution_status` tool and `/resolution status` command are the on-demand access path; no new command is required. The former `CURRENT OPERATIONAL EVIDENCE RULE`, `AUTHORITATIVE CURRENT OPERATIONAL INDEX`, SYSTEM citation catalog injection, and query-triggered `CURRENT MACHINE VALIDATION` context are retired from normal model delivery. Context-delivery receipts refresh the hidden index mechanically, and an explicit read rebuilds it from current retained evidence before