# 7.4.78.94 PYTHON DIRECT SOURCE POINTER corrects the second live 2B source-verification test, where .93 successfully selected VERIFY_SOURCE but still depended on the weak model to construct and execute an exact-source tool call. The source-verification consumer now maps VERIFY_SOURCE into a real mechanical action for retained research: Python strips only gate/control words from the user query without adding synonyms, uses the existing research keyword/archive/Pyramid navigation surfaces, follows the first existing navigation-ranked concrete pointer, executes the corresponding exact retained-source read through the normal execute_tool path so Action Snake records a genuine receipt, and delivers the bounded exact source text plus pointer/receipt metadata to Assistant before her admitted answer. Python records candidate rank/tool/pointer but explicitly has no semantic authority and does not decide whether the text supports the claim. ANSWER_UNVERIFIED and OWN_PLAN/BYPASS remain first-class escapes. Non-research or no-pointer cases retain the prior model-driven compatibility route and bounded recovery. The five-group / 116-subsystem architecture remains unchanged by advancing guided-decision-gate rev 7. Journey/checkpoint governance advances to rev 159.
# 7.4.78.93 FAILSAFE DEFAULT CHOICE GATE corrects the first live 2B source-verification test, where the weak model failed to return a valid gate choice and .92 blocked before retrieval even though VERIFY_SOURCE was the declared safe default. The reusable choice primitive now treats the caller-supplied DEFAULT as a real mechanical failsafe: any valid explicit option wins; DEFAULT explicitly selects the supplied default; OWN_PLAN/BYPASS remains a first-class escape; but after bounded malformed/ambiguous replies, or a choice-model call error, the primitive returns the supplied default with selection=default_failsafe, default_applied=true, and a mechanical fallback_reason instead of silently stopping. Invalid gate construction still fails closed because Python has no valid catalog/default to apply. The source-verification consumer therefore guides weak models onto VERIFY_SOURCE by default while preserving explicit ANSWER_UNVERIFIED and OWN_PLAN routes. Action Snake gate receipts now preserve whether the default was explicit or failsafe, the fallback reason, and choice-attempt count. This changes only mechanical routing, never semantic truth/relevance judgment, and still does not branch by model size. The five-group / 116-subsystem architecture remains unchanged by advancing guided-decision-gate rev 6. Journey/checkpoint governance advances to rev 158.
# 7.4.78.92 DEFAULT SOURCE VERIFICATION GATE is the first operational consumer of the reusable .91 choice primitive. When the current query mechanically asks to verify/check/reopen retained source evidence, the same model receives a small route gate with VERIFY_SOURCE as DEFAULT, ANSWER_UNVERIFIED as an explicit alternative, and universal OWN_PLAN/BYPASS. The gate primitive still returns only the chosen string; the source-validation caller maps that choice to turn behavior. VERIFY_SOURCE adds a compact instruction that navigation/search/signposts/keywords are not evidence and requires a successful exact-source read before the answer may describe a source as opened/verified. After the turn Python audits the already-existing encrypted Action Snake for successful exact-read tool receipts; one bounded recovery attempt is allowed if the model selected VERIFY_SOURCE but failed to execute an exact read, after which the source-verified answer is blocked rather than silently falling through. ANSWER_UNVERIFIED and OWN_PLAN remain valid bypass routes, but bypass cannot fabricate a mechanical verification receipt; explicit prose claiming a source was opened/verified without an exact-read receipt is marked ORIGINAL SOURCE NOT VERIFIED. Python does not judge whether the reopened source semantically supports the claim, choose which source is relevant, or branch by model size. The five-group / 116-subsystem architecture remains unchanged by advancing guided-decision-gate rev 5. Journey/checkpoint governance advances to rev 157.
# 7.4.78.91 REUSABLE CHOICE GATE PRIMITIVE generalizes the default-first/bypass rail pattern without adding another semantic subsystem. The existing guided-decision-gate block now exposes one small internal `run_choice_gate` primitive: a caller supplies a bounded decision prompt, mechanical facts, a list of option strings, and one default option; Python guarantees an OWN_PLAN/BYPASS route, asks the active model to choose exactly one option, tolerates simple weak-model formatting, reprompts a bounded three times, and returns only the chosen option plus mechanical trace metadata. The primitive never converts that choice into an action, executes a tool, writes state, judges relevance/truth, or branches by model size; each calling subsystem remains solely responsible for mapping its returned string to behavior. Invalid/no choice still fails without silently treating DEFAULT as consent. This is foundational infrastructure for future main-decision gates such as exact-source verification while keeping the gate itself deliberately generic and easy to audit. The five-group / 116-subsystem architecture remains unchanged by advancing guided-decision-gate rev 4. Journey/checkpoint governance advances to rev 156.
# 7.4.78.90 RESEARCH SOURCE KEYWORDS extends the mature archived-web pipeline with the narrow navigation lesson proven useful for books. Immutable research snapshots and previously selected web evidence units now receive deterministic source-word keyword baselines (12-20 words when enough distinct source vocabulary exists), stored as append-only research-navigation revisions with a tiny current head and rebuildable SQL keyword index. Assistant may revise a current list after reopening exact source; Python validates only 12-20 distinct single-word mechanics/current lineage/index refresh and does not choose or rewrite her semantic words. The existing research_run_sources.query_json remains discovery provenance (how a source was found), while navigation keywords answer only where retained source may be worth reopening. Keyword search is attempted before the established immutable local full-text/archive route, and every factual claim still requires reopening hash-verified archived readable text or exact RSC-backed evidence-unit spans. New snapshots are keyworded automatically with zero model/web calls; legacy snapshots can be backfilled explicitly with /research keywords rebuild, and prior WEUs are lazily seeded from reconstructable exact source on local unit search. No research finding, uncertainty, memory, source text, authority rank, provider behavior, or Assistant semantic judgment is changed. The five-group / 116-subsystem architecture remains stable by extending archived-web-recall rev 2 rather than creating a parallel research system. Journey/checkpoint governance advances to rev 155.
