# 7.4.78.82 NEATBOOKS-NATIVE BOOK REFLECTION SOURCE BRIDGE follows the first live `/reflect book BK-ab2e89e1a1252a95` attempt on .81. The command failed immediately even though the same Art of War source had just been reopened successfully through `read_signpost_source`, because .81 incorrectly required a duplicate row in the older `memorize_books.db` store. .82 removes that duplicate-store dependency and resolves the active digested BK-ID against the canonical NeatBooks store already used by signpost exact-source exits. Reflection metadata comes from the NeatBooks catalog; bounded session chunks are read directly from ordered `book_chunks.original_text` with original-text hashes, avoiding model-side cleanup/dedup and preserving exact source authority. Checkpoint source fingerprints use the canonical NeatBooks text/content hash, with a metadata-only ordered chunk-hash fallback for legacy rows. The existing 6-chunk/~12k soft limits, 12-chunk/20k hard ceilings, resumable progress, Assistant KEEP/REVISE_KEYWORDS authority, append-only RSR history, and source-over-signpost authority are unchanged. A regression now proves an active digested book present only in NeatBooks can enter reflection and that exact `original_text` is loaded without any `memorize_book` row. Journey/checkpoint governance advances to rev 147.
