# finalizer sat inside the record-context wrapper, while later `run_online_chat_turn` decorators
# remained free to transform or regenerate the visible answer afterward. v68.1 therefore adds a
# final presentation-boundary guard installed only after the complete runtime wrapper stack and
# query telemetry are assembled. It performs no retrieval and no writes: it takes the final visible
# online answer, validates `_ONLINE_RECORD_CONTEXT_LAST.query_key` against the exact normalized
# current user query, strips any trailing machine-owned Record-provenance footer first, and re-adds
# attribution only when that same-query packet proves actual opened `record:` refs. A regression
# explicitly simulates a stale footer being appended *after* inner finalization and verifies that the
# outer guard removes it, while a genuine same-turn record read still receives its exact attribution.
# This is fail-closed display integrity only; Research, Pyramid 7.4.67.2, retrieval, shared knowledge,
# canonical memory, citations, Assistant interpretation, and NeatTools remain unchanged.
