# 7.4.68.0 NORMAL-CHAT PROVENANCE BINDING follows repeated real ordinary-chat answers that
# ended with `[Record provenance: record:research-report:RW-20260815-201705-a25e95d6]` even when
# the current Macbeth/Odyssey turn did not use that old Research report. The persisted-record bridge
# kept one process-global `_ONLINE_RECORD_CONTEXT_LAST`; the answer finalizer appended refs from that
# mutable last packet without proving it belonged to the current user query. If a current turn did not
# replace the packet, an older record read could therefore acquire false authority over a later answer.
# v68.0 makes provenance turn-bound and fail-closed: every packet carries a normalized-query SHA-256;
# online turn entry clears prior record state before any provider/tool work; nested context builds may
# update the packet only when their query identity matches the active user turn; finalization appends a
# record footer only from a matched, current-query packet with actual opened record refs; and a stale
# trailing machine-owned `[Record provenance: ...]` footer is removed when no current binding exists.
# The public/manual finalizer no longer falls back to hidden global LAST state. Exact record reads and
# genuine research-history answers retain their required record attribution. This patch changes only
# display/binding mechanics: it does not alter Research contents, shared knowledge, citations, book
# evidence, Pyramid behavior, retrieval selection, Assistant interpretation, or any canonical memory.
# Prefer no record-provenance footer over a false one; provenance establishes source identity, not truth.
