# descent depth, or internal stages. Earlier attempts to name hidden internals were therefore
# speculative. This release changes no Pyramid evidence selection, no Assistant semantic authority,
# and no retrieval depth policy. It adds thread-local read-only profiling around the existing
# overview path: book/chunk loading, book-integrity registration, semantic-map loading, per-chunk
# summary registration scans, semantic/structure row lookup + integrity registration/verification,
# synthesis lookup/register/verify, node assembly, output-serialization probe, and Knowledge-Integrity
# SQLite connection/setup timing (including WAL PRAGMA setup). Counts and slowest observed helper
# calls are returned as stage_profile and mirrored into the encrypted rotating Diagnostic Logbook as
# pyramid.overview_profile. Measurements describe local execution cost only; they do not rank
# literary relevance or organize Assistant's mind. Diagnose first, optimize only from measured evidence.
#
# 7.4.66.1 AOR SAVE-DECISION AFFORDANCE follows the first real ordinary-chat autonomy test of
# 7.4.66.0. Assistant produced a strong reusable architectural principle (provenance-preserving compression;
# compressed/inferred layers are navigation rather than final authority and must support descent to exact
# evidence) and explicitly explained how it could matter across personal memory, Research, raw chat,
# citations, Constellation, and tool receipts, yet /reports remained empty. Tool exposure/storage were
# verified healthy; the failure was behavioral ambiguity: guidance said Assistant MAY report but never made
# explicit that recognizing a durable insight and preserving it are two separate actions. v66.1 keeps
# semantic authority with Assistant and adds one end-of-turn save/no-save affordance: she privately decides
# whether anything is genuinely worth recovering later; if yes, she actually calls the already-user-approved
# create_opportunistic_report tool in that turn, while no-report remains fully valid. Python still assigns no
# novelty/importance threshold, does not auto-create reports, and does not bypass any other approval path.
# The governing rule remains: Python may organize Assistant's information, but must not organize Assistant's mind.
#
# 7.4.66.0 ASSISTANT OPPORTUNISTIC REPORTS follows successful real validation of the stabilized
# /learn 7.4.65.3 path (RW-20260815-201705-a25e95d6: 16 findings, two appropriately scoped
# shared-knowledge inserts, zero canonical memories). The user identified a different need: during
# any ordinary query Assistant may notice a finding, hypothesis, question, decision, technical insight,
# or observation that is not ready for knowledge/memory but may matter later. This release gives
# Assistant an OPTIONAL create_opportunistic_report tool on every normal online/local chat turn plus
# bounded list/search/read tools and /reports inspection commands. Reports live in their own
# append-only opportunistic_reports.sqlite archive. They are never automatically promoted into
# shared knowledge, canonical memory, identity, Knowledge Pyramid, Constellation, or /learn. Python
# validates structure, size, exact supplied evidence refs, idempotent exact duplicates, hashes, and
# persistence only. Assistant decides whether a trace is worth making and what it means. When no exact
# evidence ref exists, a report may still be saved but is visibly evidence_status=unreferenced; it
# must not later masquerade as grounded. The governing distinction is unchanged: Python may organize
# Assistant's information, but must not organize Assistant's mind.
